== (i) the center of the reconstructed group acts by triality ==
  Lambda^1 (fundamental (quark)): center phase = omega^1 = -0.500+0.866i
  Lambda^2 (Lambda^2 (diquark)): center phase = omega^2 = -0.500-0.866i
  Lambda^3 (Lambda^3 (baryon)): center phase = omega^3 = +1.000-0.000i  -> TRIVIAL (singlet-capable)
  machine: det(omega 1_3) = +1.000-0.000i  (= 1: omega 1 is IN SU(3))

== (ii) P17's closure predicate is center neutrality ==
   base (L | R)            charges mod 3        center-neutral triple?
   [1, 4, 4]   |[2, 2, 5]     (1, 1, 1) |(2, 2, 2)    True
   [1, 5, 6]   |[2, 3, 7]     (1, 2, 0) |(2, 0, 1)    True
   [2, 5, 5]   |[3, 3, 6]     (2, 2, 2) |(0, 0, 0)    True
   [2, 6, 7]   |[3, 4, 8]     (2, 0, 1) |(0, 1, 2)    True
   [3, 6, 6]   |[4, 4, 7]     (0, 0, 0) |(1, 1, 1)    True
   [4, 7, 7]   |[5, 5, 8]     (1, 1, 1) |(2, 2, 2)    True
  -> every minimal chiral base is center-neutral as a whole (the
     P17 divisibility observation), so each closes in Z_3: the
     closure census IS the SU(3) singlet rule seen abelianly -
     as Doplicher-Roberts predicts, the abelian search detects
     exactly the CENTER of the reconstructed group.

== (iii) the lift dictionary for the multiplicity-3 spectra ==
  P17 4d minimal solutions with multiplicity-3 charges:
   {-5,-1,-1,-1, 4, 4}:  (-1)x3  ->  ONE fundamental of U(3)
                         with determinant charge -3 (= -1 each)
   {-4,-4, 1, 1, 1, 5}:  (+1)x3  ->  ONE fundamental of U(3)
                         with determinant charge +3
  -> by R3 (statistics order = fiber dimension), a multiplicity-3
     abelian charge is the SHADOW of one fiber-3 excitation; the
     abelian charge itself rides det U(3) - the hypercharge slot,
     exactly where the baryon receipt (p18c) put it.

